# Harness Vibe — choose one skill

When the user asks about Vibe, pick **exactly one** skill and follow it. Do not mix workflows in one turn.

| User intent | Skill | First tool |
|---|---|---|
| first-time / “make this repo deployable”, env/secrets, detect framework | **vibe-prepare** | none (local files). Chain **vibe-deploy** only if the user asked to deploy. |
| deploy, go live, new revision, `/vibe-deploy`, fix failed Vibe build | **vibe-deploy** | `deploy_vibe_app` **without** `confirm` |
| status, preview URL, stages, metrics, change subdomain/CDN | **vibe-status** | `get_vibe_deployment` (default) or `get_vibe_app` for metrics/settings |
| rollback production, undo last publish | **vibe-rollback** | Confirm, then `rollback_vibe_app` |

## Rules

- Never dump JSON or rebuild stages as a markdown task list. The host renders `ui://vibe/app.html`.
- Never pass `confirm: true` on `deploy_vibe_app` unless the user submitted the in-card form **or** you are redeploying after an accepted fix (see **vibe-deploy**).
- Never publish or roll back unless the user explicitly asked.
- After **vibe-prepare**, stop unless the user asked to deploy.
- Confirm before cancel; the plugin hook also asks on confirmed deploy and cancel.
- If the MCP App iframe is unavailable, use the one-line `content` summary only.

Slash commands: `/vibe-prepare`, `/vibe-deploy`, `/vibe-status`, `/vibe-rollback`. `/vibe-fix-failed-build` loads the repair section of **vibe-deploy**.
